      "writtenOn": "2026-07-24T11:52:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose we could do that like pKVM-ARM does that (as I noted above), i.e. avoid unmapping anything from the host MMU before `fix_host_mmu_pgstate()`, unmap only via the memory protection API after `fix_host_mmu_pgstate()`?\n\n\u003e it is not easy to identify this case\n\nThis `BUG_ON(!is_pvmfw_range(phys, size))` here already identifies it?\n\nSo, if doing this like pKVM-ARM does it not easy to implement right now, we may keep this BUG_ON for now (maybe just change it to an error return) and just add a FIXME, like I suggested?",
